{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"d73672952e1f1156c3f917d589d049f2bca0a39465f86c242d902a7053ba496f","digest":{"component_or_area":"inbound link differ / reconciliation","key_entities":["inbound_differ._diff_links_inbound","inbound_differ._diff_link_removals_inbound","apply_inbound_records._inbound_update_apply_links","rebar.unlink","outbound_links._diff_link_removals","binding_store","managed_refs","test_inbound_delete_link_round_trips","link_direction.resolve_inbound_link","inbound_differ.py:380,396"],"problem_keywords":["inbound link deletion not mirrored","add-only differ","asymmetric link sync","peer deletion silent failure","local ticket sync gap"],"propositions":["The inbound link differ is add-only by construction and never removes links deleted on the peer, while the outbound direction has a removal path, creating asymmetry.","A link deleted in Jira stays on the local rebar ticket forever with no pass reporting it or removing it.","The apply-layer drops all non-add link records silently (action != 'add' continues without processing), so even a correct differ emitting removals would not work.","The shipped semantics defer removal-mirroring and instead implement local-wins-and-restore: a link deleted in Jira is re-added on the next pass, converging without local data loss.","Determining whether a peer link was actually deleted versus never observed requires per-binding history of what the peer last had, which is not available in the current snapshot model."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787908203305007001,"uuid":"f3ffbe6d-8e4e-4839-8d94-5c3e4f2fc985"}